<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	`ighostvtd-remote` on the device: the remote-access helper.

	The same two keys as `ighostvt-cli`, and for the same reason — it is a
	client of the daemon and nothing more. The daemon admits it by being its
	own child (pid and path, `PeerAuthenticator`), not by the marker, but the
	marker costs nothing and keeps it inside the client rule should that
	ever change. It drops to mobile before it opens a socket, draws nothing,
	owns no container and spawns nothing, so it needs none of the app's or
	the daemon's other keys — and must not have them: it is the one process
	in this project the network can talk to.

	The one key beyond those: MobileGestalt's protected device name, which
	the helper advertises and pairs under. Without it the answer is the
	model ("iPad"), and two devices on one network cannot be told apart.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>wiki.qaq.ighostvt.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.exception.mach-lookup.global-name</key>
	<array>
		<string>wiki.qaq.ighostvt.service</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.private.MobileGestalt.AllowedProtectedKeys</key>
	<array>
		<string>UserAssignedDeviceName</string>
		<string>marketing-name</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
